# HTML semantics and layout

- Use semantic elements where they apply: `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<aside>`, `<figure>`, `<figcaption>`, form elements (`<button>`, `<input>`, `<label>`, `<fieldset>`, `<legend>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>`, `<progress>`), and list structure (`<ul>`, `<ol>`, `<li>`) instead of generic `<div>`/`<span>` when the meaning fits
- Prefer Flexbox or CSS Grid for layout; avoid layout patterns that rely on floats or table display when flex/grid are appropriate

# Template formatting

- Put **`class` first**, then list other attributes in **alphabetical order**, with **event bindings** (e.g. `(click)`) **last**
- Prefer **one attribute per line** for readability
